 "limitations": "Fit on City of Toronto street trees: managed road-allowance trees, pruned and spaced by the City. Transfer to private backyard trees is approximate. The model conditions on tree presence: P(DBH>=30 | h, area) was fit at known tree locations, so applied to a LiDAR peak it answers 'if this peak is a tree, how likely is it mature'. Peaks smoother than p5 of street-tree crown roughness are excluded as structures (flat roofs), but pitched roofs and other rough structures still pass the gate and inflate parcel rollups. Screening signal only; not a permit determination."
